# Example mesen-gdb test script, run by `make tests` from the project root.
# Each line is a debugger command; `assert` lines report PASS or FAIL.
# Commands: https://github.com/BubbleZapGames/Mesen-GDB#test-scripts
# Separate sections with `#` lines, not blank ones: a blank line repeats
# the previous command.
#
until main 60       # boot runs snes_init(), then calls main(); give it 60 frames
assert PC == main "Reached the game loop"
assert cgram 0 == 0 "snes_init cleared CGRAM"
#
# Drive the pad and check your own variables, for example:
#   input 1 right
#   frames 10
#   input 1 none
#   assert PX:u16 == 130 "Player moved right"
